WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.915 --> 00:00:07.915
Once your school gives you a seat, the next job is to build your lesson plan library. This video shows you how.

2
00:00:08.421 --> 00:00:23.501
On My Licenses, a green banner says you can pick up to forty plans. You can add more any time, but every plan you pick is permanent for your license period. So choose the ones you really plan to teach. Select Browse Lesson Plans.

3
00:00:24.007 --> 00:00:29.947
This is the full catalogue. The counter at the top shows how many plans you've added, out of your limit.

4
00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:35.999
To narrow the list, choose a grade level, pick a series, or type in the search box.

5
00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:44.543
When you find a lesson you want, select Add to Library.

6
00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:57.274
You'll see a reminder. Once a plan is added, it's a permanent part of your library, and it can't be removed. If you're not sure, select Cancel. Otherwise, select Add to My Library.

7
00:00:57.776 --> 00:01:03.186
The lesson is marked Added, and the counter goes up by one. Add the rest the same way.

8
00:01:03.688 --> 00:01:12.088
Select My Lesson Plans to see your library. Your plans are here, and you can search them, or select View Lesson to open one.

9
00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:21.990
Need more later? Select Add Plans. If your license is a trial, your limit can be lower than forty, and the counter at the top always shows it.
